# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Secrets and credential material — the important part of this file.
#
# This plugin handles live CodeArts credentials: an access key, a secret key and
# a security token. `providerLoginFile` generates `codearts-provider-<user>.json`
# for browser sign-in, and the `/export` route emits the same material as JSON.
# None of these may ever be committed.
#
# Rules are anchored to the repo root where possible so they cannot accidentally
# hide a source file deeper in the tree.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Credential files this plugin produces or imports.
/codearts-provider-*.json
/codearts-*.json
/auths/
/credentials/
/backup/
*-credentials.json
*credential*.json
*secret*.json
*token*.json

# A real gateway config (as opposed to config.example.yaml) carries the upstream
# endpoint and may carry store-source URLs.
/config.yaml
/config.yml

# Generic secret material.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
id_rsa*
.netrc
secret_key.txt

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Build and release outputs
#
# `tools/package-release.sh` writes release-assets/, and build.sh/build.bat write
# the platform library into plugins/. Binaries are distributed through GitHub
# Releases (that is what the plugin store downloads), so they do not need to be
# committed. Delete the `!` line below if you prefer to vendor the library.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/release-assets/
/plugins/**/*.dll
/plugins/**/*.so
/plugins/**/*.dylib
/plugins/**/*.h
!plugins/**/.gitkeep

# Local build scratch space.
/tools/abitest/abitest
/tools/abitest/abitest.exe
# `go build ./...` in the repo root writes an executable named after the module.
/*.exe
/dist/
/coverage.out

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Editor / IDE / OS
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Tooling state written into the working tree by the AI IDE, not by this project
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.codeartsdoer/
.codewhisperer/
.claude/
.codex/
.qoder/
.trellis/
.superpowers/
.agents/
.ace-tool/
.test_tmp/
.tmp/
.merkle-snapshot.json

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Python helpers, if any are ever added
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Logs
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.log
